# Stakeholder mail

Write Firestore `mail` (`{ to, message: { subject, html } }`) only after an explicit yes.

- Show **to, subject, HTML-as-text, ticket link, Firestore project** and wait.
- Recipients must be on the instance `mail.allowlist`. To send elsewhere, the user must retype the address.
- Run `send-stakeholder-mail.mjs` with `--confirm <token>`. No token → do not write.
- Hooks never send mail, never write `mail`, and never invent a confirm token.
- Do not use Mail.app, mailto, or a Gmail API.
- Do not log the message body, tokens, or raw PII.
- Target project must not be in `forbiddenProjects`.
